# Pod-A: two Guaranteed neighbor Pods, one per socket, 5 exclusive CPUs each.
# Light DRAM pressure with an LLC-sized working set.
#
# Guaranteed + integer CPU request means the kubelet gives these Pods their own
# exclusive cores, exactly like a real co-tenant with a CPU reservation. They
# therefore cannot steal FFmpeg's pinned CPUs - all interference is through the
# shared LLC, memory controllers, and interconnect.
#
# Reference measurement on the reference platform: 107-455 MiB LLC,
# 129-205 GB/s DRAM per pod.
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_ARGS="--stream 4
--stream-l3-size 32M
--stream-index 0
--metrics-brief
--timeout 0
--log-file stress-ng.log"
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_SCOPE=pod
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_CPU_REQUEST=5
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_MEMORY_REQUEST=16Gi
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_MEMORY_LIMIT=16Gi
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_POD_COUNT=2
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_GUARANTEED=1
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_SOCKET_SPLIT_RETRIES=3
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_REQUIRE_SOCKET_SPLIT=1
